  "fixture_kind": "original_oracle_cards",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If the creature is an illegal target when Rapid Hybridization tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. No Frog Lizard token will be created.",
      "oracle_id": "06692cd9-ac2f-4a32-8fd1-043ba3c0fe71",
      "published_at": "2013-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Rapid Hybridization resolves and the creature isn't destroyed (perhaps because it has indestructible), its controller will still get the Frog Lizard token.",
      "oracle_id": "06692cd9-ac2f-4a32-8fd1-043ba3c0fe71",
      "published_at": "2013-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Incongruity tries to resolve, the spell doesn't resolve. No player creates a Frog Lizard token.",
      "oracle_id": "363edb16-009f-4cc2-99e3-2b15db84e7af",
      "published_at": "2019-01-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A split card's characteristics are a combination of its two halves while it is not on the stack. For example, Assault // Battery has a mana value of 5 while it is in your library. If an effect allows you to search your library for a card with mana value 4 or less, you can't find Assault // Battery.",
      "oracle_id": "363edb16-009f-4cc2-99e3-2b15db84e7af",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each split card is a single card. For example, if you discard a split card, you've discarded one card, not two. If an effect counts the number of sorcery cards in your graveyard, Assault // Battery counts once, not twice.",
      "oracle_id": "363edb16-009f-4cc2-99e3-2b15db84e7af",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To cast a split card, choose one of its halves to cast. There's no way to cast both halves of this split card.",
      "oracle_id": "363edb16-009f-4cc2-99e3-2b15db84e7af",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect allows you to cast a spell with certain characteristics, consider only the characteristics of the half you're casting. For example, if an effect allows you to cast a sorcery spell with mana value 2 or less from among cards in your graveyard, you could cast Assault this way, but not Battery.",
      "oracle_id": "363edb16-009f-4cc2-99e3-2b15db84e7af",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you copy a spell that's half of a split card, the copy copies that same half. For example, if you copy Assault, the copy is also Assault, not Battery.",
      "oracle_id": "363edb16-009f-4cc2-99e3-2b15db84e7af",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each split card has two names. If an effect instructs you to choose a card name, you may choose one of those names, but not both.",
      "oracle_id": "363edb16-009f-4cc2-99e3-2b15db84e7af",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Split cards have two card faces on a single card. The characteristics of the half you didn't cast are ignored while the spell is on the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "363edb16-009f-4cc2-99e3-2b15db84e7af",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the target noncreature permanent is an illegal target by the time Sawtusk Demolisher\u2019s last ability tries to resolve, the ability won\u2019t resolve. No player will create a Beast token. If the target is legal but not destroyed (most likely because it has indestructible), its controller does create a Beast token.",
      "oracle_id": "7f93a368-9568-456c-9bd6-20d5fe5ad2f1",
      "published_at": "2020-04-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the target artifact becomes illegal before resolution, the player does not gain any life.",
      "oracle_id": "8d6e39b0-a190-40a0-a8e1-ee82f477376f",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn\u2019t provide any additional benefit.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it\u2019s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don\u2019t grant bonuses to your opponents\u2019 Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this creature enters at the same time as one or more other creatures, its ability will trigger for each of those other creatures. ",
      "oracle_id": "f3fad295-1af2-4ecc-8546-b121ad6be27b",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
